Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 47, verse 7:

His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿O you who have believed, if you support Allah, He will support you and plant firmly your feet.﴾ In this noble verse, Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, mentions that if the believers support their Lord, He will support them against their enemies and make their feet firm, meaning He will preserve them from flight and defeat.

This meaning has been made clear in many verses, and in some of them He has explained the attributes of those to whom He promised this victory:

• Such as His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿Allah will surely support those who support Him. Indeed, Allah is Powerful and Exalted in Might﴾ [al-Hajj: 40], and then He explained the attributes of those promised this victory in His saying after it: ﴿those who, if We establish them in the land, establish prayer, give zakah, enjoin what is right, and forbid what is wrong. And with Allah is the outcome of all matters﴾ [al-Hajj: 41];

• And such as His saying: ﴿And it was incumbent upon Us to support the believers﴾ [ar-Rum: 47];

• And His saying: ﴿Indeed, We will surely support Our messengers and those who believe in the worldly life﴾ [Ghafir: 51];

• And His saying: ﴿And已 Our word had already preceded to Our servants, the messengers. Indeed, they would be the ones given victory. And indeed, Our soldiers – they would be the predominant﴾ [as-Saffat: 171–173];

and to other verses besides these.

(p-252) And His saying, in describing the attributes of those whom He promised victory in the aforementioned verses: ﴿those who, if We establish them in the land, establish prayer, give zakah, and enjoin what is right﴾ [al-Hajj: 41].

This indicates that those who do not establish prayer, do not give zakah, do not enjoin what is right, and do not forbid what is wrong, have no promise from Allah of victory whatsoever.

Their example is like the example of the hired worker who did not do any work for his employer, then came to him seeking his wage.

As for those who commit all sins among those who name themselves by the name of Muslims, then say: "Allah will surely give us victory" – they are deluded, because they are not of the party of Allah who are promised His victory, as is not hidden.

The meaning of the believers supporting Allah is: their support of His religion and His Book, and their striving and jihad so that His word is supreme, His limits are established on His earth, His commands are obeyed and His prohibitions avoided, and judgment is made among His servants by what He sent down upon His Messenger (ﷺ).
